---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="What to Expect | Rooted Tides"
  description="What happens in a Reiki session, what you might feel, and answers to common questions."
  canonical="/expect"
>
  <div class="container section">
    <h1>What to Expect</h1>
    <p class="small">
      Sessions are calm, quiet, and supportive. You’ll be fully clothed and comfortable on a treatment table
      (or seated if preferred).
    </p>

    <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top:22px;">
      <div class="card" style="padding:22px;">
        <h2>How a session flows</h2>
        <ol class="small" style="margin:0; padding-left:18px;">
          <li><strong>Arrival + intention (2–5 min)</strong> — a gentle check-in</li>
          <li><strong>Reiki (45–55 min)</strong> — hands-on or hands-near, based on consent</li>
          <li><strong>Closing (2–5 min)</strong> — slow transition, optional brief reflection</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 style="margin-top:18px;">What you might feel</h2>
        <p class="small">
          Everyone’s different. You might notice warmth, tingling, emotional release, deep calm, or simply rest.
          Some people feel subtle changes immediately; others notice shifts over the next day or two.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card" style="padding:22px;">
        <h2>FAQ</h2>

        <h3>Do I have to believe in Reiki?</h3>
        <p class="small">No. Many people simply come for quiet, nervous-system settling, and rest.</p>

        <h3>What should I wear?</h3>
        <p class="small">Comfortable clothing. You stay fully clothed.</p>

        <h3>Is this medical treatment?</h3>
        <p class="small">Reiki is a complementary wellness practice and is not a substitute for medical care.</p>

        <h3>How many sessions should I book?</h3>
        <p class="small">
          One session can be deeply relaxing. Packages are helpful if you want ongoing support or a steadier rhythm.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
